Support `[tool.uv.sources] pkg = { url = "..." }` in uv.lock

When a package is sourced from a URL (e.g. a GitHub archive tarball),
uv writes:

    source = { url = "..." }
    sdist = { hash = "sha256:..." }

Note that `sdist` has no `url` — the URL lives at the source level.
The stock uv_translator.py assumes every wheel/sdist entry carries a
`url` or `file` field, so it raises AssertionError:

    File "pycross/private/tools/uv_translator.py", line 121, in parse_file_info
        raise AssertionError("file entry has no file or url member")

This patch propagates `source.url` into the sdist entry before file
parsing, so URL-sourced packages resolve the same way PyPI-sourced
ones do. The tarball's sha256 comes straight from uv.lock — committed
at `uv lock` time, verified by Bazel's http_file at download time; no
translation-time network access.

Additionally, URL sources need not have a PEP 517-shaped basename:
GitHub archive tarballs are named `<sha>.tar.gz`, which
packaging.utils.parse_sdist_filename rejects. For such URLs the patch
synthesizes a canonical `<name>-<version>.tar.gz` file name (carried
via a `_pycross_filename` field honored by parse_file_info). The
download URL is unchanged — only Bazel-side target/file naming uses
the synthesized name.

Used for e.g. PyKMIP (mongodb-forks fork consumed as a GitHub archive
tarball) and the mdb-build-public cryptography wheels.

Applied in mongo repo via `single_version_override(patches=...)` on
rules_pycross in //MODULE.bazel. Candidate for upstreaming to
jvolkman/rules_pycross.

--- a/pycross/private/tools/uv_translator.py	2026-07-21 15:01:26
+++ b/pycross/private/tools/uv_translator.py	2026-07-21 15:01:50
@@ -114,8 +114,15 @@
         urls = tuple()
     elif "url" in file_info:
         url = file_info["url"]
-        _, file_name = urlparse(url).path.rsplit("/", 1)
-        file_name = unquote(file_name)
+        if "_pycross_filename" in file_info:
+            # Set for URL sources whose basename isn't a valid
+            # PEP 517 sdist filename (e.g. GitHub /archive/<sha>.tar.gz).
+            # The URL is still downloaded verbatim; this only controls the
+            # local/canonical file name.
+            file_name = file_info["_pycross_filename"]
+        else:
+            _, file_name = urlparse(url).path.rsplit("/", 1)
+            file_name = unquote(file_name)
         urls = (url,)
     else:
         raise AssertionError("file entry has no file or url member")
@@ -367,9 +374,37 @@
 
             dependencies.add(Requirement(dep_string))
 
+        # When a package is sourced via `[tool.uv.sources] pkg = { url = ... }`,
+        # uv writes `source = { url = "..." }` at the package level and
+        # `sdist = { hash = "..." }` without a url (the source URL doubles as
+        # the sdist URL). parse_file_info() below rejects any file entry
+        # without a url; propagate source.url into the sdist entry here so
+        # URL-sourced packages behave the same as PyPI-sourced ones.
+        _source = lock_pkg.get("source", {})
+        _sdist_raw = lock_pkg.get("sdist")
+        if (
+            isinstance(_sdist_raw, dict)
+            and "url" not in _sdist_raw
+            and "file" not in _sdist_raw
+            and isinstance(_source, dict)
+            and isinstance(_source.get("url"), str)
+        ):
+            _sdist_raw = dict(_sdist_raw, url=_source["url"])
+            # URL sources need not have a PEP 517-shaped basename (e.g.
+            # GitHub archive tarballs are named `<sha>.tar.gz`). Downstream
+            # parsing (packaging.utils.parse_sdist_filename) requires
+            # `<name>-<version>.tar.gz`, so synthesize that shape when the
+            # basename doesn't already carry it. The download URL is
+            # unchanged — only the canonical file name differs.
+            _, _url_basename = urlparse(_source["url"]).path.rsplit("/", 1)
+            _expected_prefix = f"{package_name}-{package_version}"
+            if not unquote(_url_basename).lower().startswith(_expected_prefix.lower()):
+                _sdist_raw["_pycross_filename"] = f"{_expected_prefix}.tar.gz"
+            lock_pkg = dict(lock_pkg, sdist=_sdist_raw)
+
         files = lock_pkg.get("wheels", [])
         if lock_pkg.get("sdist"):
-            files.append(lock_pkg.get("sdist"))
+            files.append(_sdist_raw if _sdist_raw is not None else lock_pkg.get("sdist"))
 
         files = {parse_file_info(f) for f in files}
 
